      "why": "iterative is the lowest-power family (single shared datapath, no per-stage registers), so it is the only candidate that can plausibly minimise power_index. It produces 1 result per (N+3) cycles, so to hit 50 MSPS it needs Fmax >= 50*(N+3) MHz; with N in 12..16 that is 750..1000 MHz, which is far beyond sky130 sc_hd, so the throughput constraint will force the search to the low-N end of the range. I keep n_iter 12..16 so the accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) is still reachable while the cost model can find the smallest N that satisfies it; data_width 14..18 and the guard bits give the accuracy trade-off room, and both rounding modes are kept since rounding can change the achievable accuracy_bits at a given N."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": 0,
          "param": "frac_guard"
        },
