{
  "decision": "infeasible",
  "rationale": "The throughput constraint (>= 50 MSPS) is unreachable with the explored families. The iterative and unrolled_k architectures are latency-bound (N+3 and ceil(N/k)+3 cycles respectively), resulting in a maximum observed throughput of only 16.1 MSPS (unrolled_k) and 11.5 MSPS (iterative). This is a factor of ~3-4x below the required 50 MSPS. To achieve 50 MSPS, a pipelined architecture (1 result/cycle) is required, but the pipelined and pipelined_m families have not been explored in the 100 evaluations used so far. Since this is the final round and no feasible design has been found, and the current best throughput is far from the target, the spec is infeasible within the current exploration scope and budget."
